Ladybird creates the wrappers for a frame’s Navigation object and its
NavigateEvents in the frame’s own realm, whichever realm’s script first
gets them. WebKit does the same for events: JSEventListener::
handleEvent() wraps the event with toJS() for the global object of the
target’s script execution context, not the listener’s. And Blink never
creates such a wrapper twice: Its ScriptWrappable keeps its main-world
wrapper, main_world_wrapper_, for as long as the object lives.
